<newsitem itemid="44939" id="root" date="1996-09-10" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Newman Tonks H1 pretax profit slips.</title>
<headline>Newman Tonks H1 pretax profit slips.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence) (adjusted) 1.91		   vs 5.11</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.625		  vs 2.90</p>
<p> Pretax		     6.5		    vs 10.7</p>
<p> Turnover		   126.4		  vs 116.2</p>
<p> Operating result	 7.8		    vs 11.8</p>
<p> Interest		   1.3		    vs 1.1</p>
<p> Tax			  2.8		    vs 3.4</p>
<p> Net taxed		  3.7		    vs 7.3</p>
<p> Attributable	     3.5		    vs 7.2</p>
<p> Pay date		   October 25</p>
<p>Div registration date  September 24</p>
<p>NOTE - Building products company Newman Tonks Group Plc said it would pay the interim dividend as a Foreign Income Dividend (FID) but did not expect to pay the final dividend as a FID.</p>
<p>The company said it expected the current trend of improvement in the U.S. to continue at least into 1997.</p>
<p>In Europe, it expects to grow market share in Germany and France while in the UK there was little evidence that conditions would improve substantially, Newman Tonks said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
